; A nullary primitive is read by naming it: `__resource_unwinding`
; with no parentheses is the operation, as the head of an application
; is. So it counts toward the lexical `Unsafe` obligation
; (docs/memory-model.md MM-EXEC-9d) both ways.
;
; Accepted: `unwinding` claims `effect(unsafe)` and reads the
; primitive, so its claim guards that read.
;
; Refused with AX3073: `untagged` reads the same primitive without the
; tag.
;@axiom:effect(unsafe)
(:: unwinding Bool)
(fn (unwinding) (== __resource_unwinding 1))

(:: untagged Bool)
(fn (untagged) (== __resource_unwinding 1))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main) 0)
